{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ef core change tracking and persistence ef core change tracking and persistence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence.md","fileName":"EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Entity Framework Core Data Access]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Access","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ef core change tracking and persistence ef core change tracking and persistence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence.md","fileName":"EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence","heading":"EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An EF Core context tracks the state of entity instances as unchanged, added, modified, or deleted. Property changes and relationship changes become a set of database commands when `SaveChanges` or its asynchronous counterpart is called.\n\nTracking supports convenient unit-of-work behavior, but it consumes memory and can preserve stale state in a long-lived context. Read-only queries can disable tracking when entity updates are not needed.\n\nEntity Framework tracks materialized entities so changes can later be translated into insert, update, or delete commands when `SaveChanges` or its asynchronous form executes. Tracking connects object mutation to persistence but also creates a defined context lifetime and state boundary.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Access","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ef core change tracking and persistence ef core change tracking and persistence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence.md","fileName":"EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"EF Core Change Tracking and Persistence","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Access","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}